# .gitattributes - line endings are pinned here, not left to whatever last wrote the file.
#
# ⚠️ WHY THIS EXISTS. Three hand files were silently flipped between CRLF and LF during one
# session's work. `"\n".join(lines)` forces LF. csv.writer does the opposite: its lineterminator
# defaults to "\r\n", so any script that rewrites a CSV through it converts the whole file. Neither
# changed a single character of content, and both turned a small edit into a whole-file rewrite:
# hand_links.csv diffed at 22,226 lines against a real change of 1,694. The first diagnosis blamed
# row ordering and restoring the original order changed the diff by exactly zero lines.
#
# With the rules below git normalizes on the way in, so a script may write whatever it likes and the
# committed diff still shows only the lines that actually changed.

# Everything text is LF in the repository and LF in the working tree.
* text=auto eol=lf

# ⚠️ CAPTURED WEB PAGES ARE EVIDENCE AND ARE FROZEN BYTE FOR BYTE. They are what a real site
# actually served, and the importer's fixtures exist to prove the reader handles that page as it
# was. Normalizing them would edit the record. Four of them carry CRLF today and keep it.
tests/fixtures/pages/** -text

# Binary, never normalized and never diffed as text.
*.woff2 binary
*.xlsx  binary
*.db    binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.heic  binary
*.webp  binary
